  "requestTimestamp": "2026-07-19T05:58:23.088Z",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nYes, a self-employed individual is required to file an annual income tax return. This obligation is established under Section 51 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC).\n\n### Controlling Authorities\n- **NIRC Section 51**: This section outlines the requirements for individuals to file income tax returns, specifying that every Filipino citizen residing in the Philippines, as well as those residing outside the Philippines on income derived from sources within the country, must file a return.\n\n### Interpretation\nSection 51 of the NIRC mandates that individuals, including self-employed persons, must file an income tax return annually. This requirement applies regardless of the amount of income earned, as long as the individual is engaged in a trade or business. The law does not provide exemptions for self-employed individuals based on income thresholds, thus reinforcing the obligation to report income and pay taxes accordingly.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor self-employed individuals, this means they must maintain accurate records of their income and expenses throughout the year to ensure compliance with tax filing requirements. They must file their income tax return on or before the 15th day of April each year, covering the income earned in the previous taxable year. Failure to file can result in penalties and interest on unpaid taxes, emphasizing the importance of timely and accurate tax reporting.",
